 from interviews of miyamoto  moving on the same trope that was used  in the donkey kong super mario brothers  franchise of a damsel in distress which  the hero must save which by the way was  literally based off of the popeye  cartoon was also used in the legend of  zelda because let's face it we all want  to play as a hero who has to save  somebody when coming up with the idea  for who link would have to save though  it was actually a public relations agent  working for nintendo at the time that  suggested that the character of the  woman needing saving would be a lady of  eternal beauty kind of a legendary  concept in and of itself they wanted to  come up with a name that sounded like a  legendary beauty but instead of  fabricating one the same agent then  suggested that they use the unique name  of the wife of a famous american author  known as f scott fitzgerald she was a  woman who was known for her beauty and  being an author and dancer and her name  was zelda and thus princess zelda was  created her visual design doesn't have  any spectacular or specific details as  to why she ended up initially being a  redhead wearing a pink dress but we can  only assume that her coloration was  decided upon in order to contrast with  the green of link or the blue of ganon  and what a crafty segue into talking  about the creation of ganon see once  upon a time in austin texas a mommy  akita and a daddy akita loved each other  very much and ganon was created then i  drove down and paid a lot of money to oh  oh sorry wrong ganon the original ganon  from the legend of zelda was created  because the game needed a villain  obviously but instead of going the same  route that mario did with the king  kong-ish big monkey donkey kong just  kind of blindly wanting to steal a lady  away they felt that because zelda was  more of an adventure and had a bigger  concentration on good versus evil the  villain needed to be someone a bit more  sinister and you know evil his original  name w